# docs/installation.md

# ADMFL Installation Guide

## System Requirements

Recommended environment:

- Ubuntu 22.04
- Python 3.10+
- Docker
- Mininet
- BMv2
- Ryu Controller

---

# Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/ADMFL.git

cd ADMFL
```

---

# Create Virtual Environment

```bash
python3 -m venv admfl_env

source admfl_env/bin/activate
```

---

# Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install --upgrade pip

pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

# Install Docker

```bash
sudo apt install docker.io docker-compose
```

---

# Verify Installation

```bash
python run.py
```

---

# Docker Deployment

## Build Containers

```bash
docker-compose build
```

## Run Framework

```bash
docker-compose up
```

---

# Running Experiments

```bash
bash scripts/run_experiments.sh
```

---

# Running Tests

```bash
pytest tests/
```

---

# Common Issues

## Missing Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Permission Denied

```bash
chmod +x scripts/*.sh
chmod +x p4/*.sh
```

---

# ADMFL Ready

The framework is now ready for experimentation.